{
  "tema": 7059,
  "slug": "me-gustaria",
  "titulo": "Using gustar in the conditional = would like",
  "subtitulo": "Me gustaría ir, ¿te gustaría venir?: the polite way to want.",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "Would like = indirect pronoun + gustaría (only this form) + infinitive: me gustaría, te gustaría, le gustaría, nos gustaría, les gustaría.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The most common way to say _would like (to do something)_ is **gustar** in the **conditional**. Only the 3rd person singular form, **gustaría**, is used with an infinitive."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "**me / te / le / nos / les**",
            "**gustaría**",
            "infinitive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "English",
            "Spanish"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "I would like",
              "me gustaría"
            ],
            [
              "you would like",
              "te gustaría"
            ],
            [
              "he / she / you (usted) would like",
              "le gustaría"
            ],
            [
              "we would like",
              "nos gustaría"
            ],
            [
              "they / you all would like",
              "les gustaría"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Gustar** is a reverse verb: the person goes in the **indirect object pronoun** (**me**, **te**, **le**…), not as the subject."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "After **gustaría** comes an **infinitive**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "A common mistake is to use a subject pronoun: **yo gustaría** ✗. To add emphasis, use **a mí**: **a mí me gustaría**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: before an infinitive, **gustaría** never changes; the pronoun in front tells you who wants it. (Before a plural noun it does: **me gustarían unos tacos**.)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Este año ==me gustaría== tomar un curso de fotografía.",
              "en": "This year I'd like to take a photography class."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿==Te gustaría== conocer a mis papás? —No, gracias.",
              "en": "\"Would you like to meet my parents?\" \"No, thanks.\""
            },
            {
              "es": "A Naomi ==le gustaría== viajar a la Tierra.",
              "en": "Naomi would like to travel to Earth."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Nos gustaría== inscribirnos a clases de salsa.",
              "en": "We'd like to sign up for salsa classes."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Les gustaría== hacer una gran fiesta de aniversario.",
              "en": "They'd like to throw a big anniversary party."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Les gustaría== participar en la encuesta?",
              "en": "Would you like to take part in the survey?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
